WEBVTT

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:06.260
Standing before the presence
of the dragon gods...

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:09.270
I humbly speak these words.

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:11.930
Please accept this branch offering.

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:16.310
Let me hear the name
of the chosen Key Girl.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:20.190
I humbly speak these words.

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:28.580
Is it decided?

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.000
For the upcoming Ritual...

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:34.920
the Key Girl is...

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:25.570
Anastomosis, eh?

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:30.110
To think that once they know love,
they can no longer ride the OTF.

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:33.910
Training them to stay away
from the male groups to start with

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:36.750
wasn't an option either.

00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:40.370
If we had, we could've
been saved a lot of trouble.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:42.130
According to Ceremony Official Iboshi,

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:46.880
Love is like an infectious disease
that's bound to be contracted someday.

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:52.800
To make them believe that their only
reason is their bond with the OTF,

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:55.140
love is rather necessary.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:03:00.310
Force the Dragon Pilots to fall in love
once, then shatter it into pieces.

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:01.980
He said that to himself before.

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:04.190
That's one thing we can't do.

00:03:04.270 --> 00:03:06.070
Are you a mother bear
and they your cubs?

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:08.400
Aside from Senior Master Sergeant Hoshino,

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:12.660
Technical Sergeant Amakasu was unaware
of her love towards Okonogi.

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:14.780
To break up their love,

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:18.330
they must realize those feelings
exist in the first place.

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:20.960
What you think will happen?

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:24.540
It'll go the wrong way.

00:03:24.710 --> 00:03:26.920
Definitely the wrong way.

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:33.220
Oh dear. Also with the Ritual
just around the corner.

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:39.680
Are we really doing this?

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:42.850
Letting the C-1 force landing
on the carrier.

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:47.860
To simulate landing on Lord Mitatsu,
this training is indispensable.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:51.240
Don't worry.
If anyone can do it, it's them.

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:17.010
We did it, Futomomo.

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:18.640
Yes, but...

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:22.020
-somehow it doesn't feel right.
-What <i>do you mean?</i>

00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:26.520
Futomomo seems a little down... somehow.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:30.530
Probably because Masotan
and Norma aren't here.

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:34.910
It's much more fun flying with everyone.

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:38.080
You're lonely, aren't you, Futomomo?

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:55.300
Ah, I'm so damn tired.

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:58.390
-The ones weak to love?
-Women are such trouble.

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:00.640
You're just jealous, aren't you?

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:03.310
Oddly enough, even men like gossip.

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:05.690
-I'm pathetic.
-El?

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:10.690
Why do I feel like this?
I want to dig it up and pull it out.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:13.190
That sounds like from
a gory, splatter film...

00:05:13.940 --> 00:05:15.240
A bystander, huh?

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:18.200
You're in the middle
of this scandal too, right?

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:21.450
Yeah, for the most part, but...

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.300
The hell was that?

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:37.720
Why doesn't High Steward Okonogi
reject her?

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:40.350
It's supposed to be
a sacred place of business!

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:43.270
Doesn't it piss you off, Amakasu?

00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:46.020
W-Why would it?

00:05:47.270 --> 00:05:49.060
You do act like a bystander.

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:55.940
-Nao.
-Huh?

00:05:56.450 --> 00:05:58.740
Can I ask you for another favor?

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:02.740
Masotan.

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:04.700
Masotan!

00:06:08.210 --> 00:06:09.790
Masotan!

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:22.350
Oh yeah.

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:23.760
That's right.

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:25.310
I'm sorry.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:28.230
It's the anastomosis.

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:31.770
To put it another way,
it's like the OTF is jealous.

00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:35.820
Like he can't accept someone else taking
his pilot's attention away from him.

00:06:36.820 --> 00:06:40.820
That time, I could sense
that Masotan was confused.

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:44.240
He couldn't understand.

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:48.080
I don't understand it myself.

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:51.000
Me being in love with Okonogi...

00:06:51.380 --> 00:06:53.840
and being unable to ride
Masotan if I fall in love.

00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:58.840
There's so much I don't understand that
I don't even know how to think.

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:01.340
I'm so sorry, Masotan!

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:05.430
It's all my fault! I'm really sorry!

00:07:07.980 --> 00:07:09.100
Change?

00:07:09.940 --> 00:07:12.600
My mama used to ride the OTF.

00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:16.570
I don't know I was affected
or brainwashed by that,

00:07:16.940 --> 00:07:20.700
but my feelings about wanting
to be a Dragon Pilot...

00:07:21.110 --> 00:07:23.620
are starting to change.

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:27.790
So you took this path
only because of your mom?

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:29.710
No, that's wrong.

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:32.040
I really respect Mama...

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:35.670
but I couldn't ride Masotan.

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:39.760
Which means you don't rely much
on others, Kaizaki.

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:40.880
Huh?

00:07:41.050 --> 00:07:43.390
Physically, you're a junior size...

00:07:43.590 --> 00:07:46.810
but you've got the mind
of a mature, independent woman.

00:07:46.930 --> 00:07:49.020
That sounds like a compliment.

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:52.190
On paper I might be a Dragon Pilot...

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:54.480
but I can't fly.

00:07:55.860 --> 00:07:58.280
So, I thought if I assisted
with Masotan's maintenance...

00:07:59.110 --> 00:08:03.280
then maybe, little by little,
I'd know more about how he felt.

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:08.490
And, I started thinking
of him to be cute.

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:12.040
Though I don't adore him
like Amakasu does.

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:17.840
I think it's the hardest on Masotan,
not letting Amakasu ride him.

00:08:18.460 --> 00:08:23.430
But it must be incredibly hard for Amakasu
to just stand by and watch.

00:08:24.930 --> 00:08:25.800
Mr. Ikushima?

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:28.850
I too felt it was time...

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:31.480
to make a junior size for you, Kaizaki.

00:08:32.390 --> 00:08:33.230
Huh?

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:39.570
Hey.

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:42.570
How you've been feeling?

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:44.700
What do you think?

00:08:45.070 --> 00:08:48.450
Since the anastomosis deal,
I haven't been able to board Norma.

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:56.040
You really got me there, Hoshino.
I mean, El.

00:08:56.250 --> 00:08:58.500
You're pretty vulnerable to love.

00:08:58.630 --> 00:09:03.050
I never thought you'd fall head over heels
'cause I was a little nice to you.

00:09:03.130 --> 00:09:06.550
You've got a nice body,
so I just thought I'd play around.

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:08.430
What a waste!

00:09:09.510 --> 00:09:11.930
I'll happily be friends with benefits
with you.

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:14.020
But nothing serious.
Give me a break--

00:09:20.650 --> 00:09:21.480
Unforgivable.

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:27.490
I'll never forgive myself for being
charmed by you for even one moment!

00:09:34.660 --> 00:09:36.960
I want you to reject El Hoshino...

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:39.460
to the point where
she swears off men.

00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:43.800
I want you to act like your whirlwind
infatuation has vanished.

00:09:44.510 --> 00:09:46.510
I can't do that.

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:49.390
I can't hurt Senior Master
Sergeant Hoshino on purpose.

00:09:49.890 --> 00:09:52.810
Then you're okay with
letting her dream die?

00:09:53.970 --> 00:09:59.150
If Senior Master Sergeant Hoshino
withdraws from her mission now...

00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:03.400
I think you can understand.

00:10:06.150 --> 00:10:09.410
<i>You will become a fighter pilot, Hoshino.</i>

00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:13.620
<i>You were ridiculed but made it</i>
<i>this far 'cause you never gave up.</i>

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:16.870
<i>That's why your dream...</i>

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:19.000
<i>will absolutely come true.</i>

00:10:20.290 --> 00:10:22.790
Friends with benefits, my ass!

00:10:23.630 --> 00:10:28.430
I will protect my purity with all my life!

00:10:28.630 --> 00:10:30.510
-Your voice is loud.
-Filthy men!

00:10:30.590 --> 00:10:31.800
Thanks for waiting.

00:10:32.140 --> 00:10:34.850
Here's another filthy man! Get away!

00:10:35.890 --> 00:10:39.980
This is soaked in salt and spice
and it's filthy! Good and bad!

00:10:41.770 --> 00:10:44.070
Delicious, but filthy.

00:10:44.150 --> 00:10:45.820
I'll need some liquor!

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:47.530
Please excuse her.

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:51.570
There's not enough booze!

00:10:55.910 --> 00:10:58.460
El, let's sleep in our room.

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:00.330
Please go ahead first.

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:02.000
I'll take her back.

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:03.130
But...

00:11:03.210 --> 00:11:06.000
Well, you both are sneaky badgers.

00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:09.680
It might be best
to lick your wounds tonight.

00:11:10.340 --> 00:11:11.840
All right, be careful.

00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:32.200
How about some <i>Joie?</i>

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:35.530
Ms. Sada! You're selling <i>Joie</i>
at this hour?

00:11:36.030 --> 00:11:39.200
I shouldn't change the pace
at which I've been going.

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:42.170
Or I'd lose sight of myself, right?

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:45.670
Lose sight of yourself?

00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:49.630
I had someone I cared about, too.

00:11:49.970 --> 00:11:50.800
Really?

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:53.640
Then what happened with that person?

00:11:54.050 --> 00:11:57.310
People...
Well, not just people.

00:11:57.510 --> 00:12:00.680
The world, the system,
all of it can betray you.

00:12:01.060 --> 00:12:01.890
Huh?

00:12:02.230 --> 00:12:03.650
It's obvious, isn't it?

00:12:04.100 --> 00:12:06.480
Each person is different.

00:12:07.020 --> 00:12:10.150
No one can understand another
in a pure way.

00:12:10.490 --> 00:12:12.240
-Then?
-You know...

00:12:13.450 --> 00:12:17.200
only Organic Transformed Fliers
will not betray you.

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:22.410
And so, in return we must not betray them.

00:12:22.750 --> 00:12:24.750
-So that means...
-Norma.

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:28.340
Norma... is my everything.

00:12:28.710 --> 00:12:29.840
El...

00:12:30.210 --> 00:12:35.430
Why did my heart move
for someone other than Norma?

00:12:36.140 --> 00:12:38.890
I will not betray Norma.

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:40.970
I will live for my dream!

00:12:41.310 --> 00:12:44.310
I want to fly anywhere
and everywhere with Norma!

00:12:46.100 --> 00:12:47.610
Right. You pass.

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:52.740
Thanks for the drink!

00:12:56.200 --> 00:13:00.290
<i>I thought that Ms. Sada's story</i>
<i>was a very good one.</i>

00:13:01.410 --> 00:13:03.000
<i>But, I wonder why?</i>

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:06.830
<i>Why am I not convinced?</i>

00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:12.550
<i>Hiso Maso!</i>

00:13:14.010 --> 00:13:16.510
PLEASE KEEP THE RESTROOM CLEAN

00:13:16.930 --> 00:13:20.470
<i>Maybe I shouldn't run from Okonogi.</i>

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:25.940
<i>I need to face him properly</i>
<i>and verify my feelings.</i>

00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:31.440
<i>Why am I brushing</i>
<i>more meticulously than usual?</i>

00:13:35.990 --> 00:13:37.200
-Haru.
-Hmm?

00:13:38.110 --> 00:13:38.950
Kiss me.

00:13:39.990 --> 00:13:40.830
Huh?

00:13:40.910 --> 00:13:45.000
When I was in fifth grade, we were eating
Ozoni soup on New Year's.

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:46.040
O-Ozoni?

00:13:46.370 --> 00:13:51.750
You said then that you'd grant my wish
if I were chosen as the Key Girl.

00:13:52.050 --> 00:13:53.510
So, grant me my wish, now.

00:13:54.010 --> 00:13:55.010
Now?

00:13:55.550 --> 00:13:57.550
Would you lie to a fifth grader?

00:13:58.640 --> 00:13:59.550
Hurry up.

00:13:59.970 --> 00:14:01.140
Do it.

00:14:08.440 --> 00:14:11.570
Why are you breathing on me!
Ugh, you stink of smoke.

00:14:17.450 --> 00:14:18.410
Haru?

00:14:18.860 --> 00:14:22.580
Sorry, for some reason...
your tear glands weaken, as you age.

00:14:23.830 --> 00:14:24.660
You idiot.

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:26.910
Sorry.

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:30.040
But Natsume, if you don't
want to be the Key Girl--

00:14:30.130 --> 00:14:31.670
What? That's stupid.

00:14:32.090 --> 00:14:34.800
I was born for the Ritual.

00:14:35.050 --> 00:14:37.670
I have worked hard to be the Key Girl.

00:14:38.170 --> 00:14:39.430
Why wouldn't I do it?

00:14:39.840 --> 00:14:40.680
That's stupid!

00:14:42.970 --> 00:14:43.930
Yes, you're right.

00:14:46.390 --> 00:14:47.230
Sorry.

00:14:49.310 --> 00:14:51.310
<i>For a long time...</i>

00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:53.690
<i>I took everything for granted.</i>

00:14:54.820 --> 00:14:55.690
<i>But...</i>

00:14:56.150 --> 00:14:58.950
<i>what other people accept as normal...</i>

00:14:59.320 --> 00:15:01.700
<i>are things that Amakasu</i>
<i>fret and struggle over.</i>

00:15:02.320 --> 00:15:06.160
<i>When I saw her search for answers</i>
<i>that were only right for her...</i>

00:15:07.160 --> 00:15:11.880
<i>I realized that maybe there is</i>
<i>nothing normal to be found.</i>

00:15:13.880 --> 00:15:15.550
You miss Amakasu, don't you?

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:16.840
Masotan.

00:15:18.130 --> 00:15:19.050
Masotan!

00:15:23.050 --> 00:15:24.350
Amakasu?

00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:27.600
You are just like me!

00:15:28.520 --> 00:15:30.690
Whenever something happens,
you consult Masotan!

00:15:31.140 --> 00:15:33.480
To think that Masotan
will accept everything about you

00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:35.400
is much too naive, Okonogi!

00:15:36.070 --> 00:15:38.440
But right now I want you
to give up your rights

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:40.570
to consult Masotan!

00:15:41.240 --> 00:15:43.030
Rights to consult?

00:15:43.110 --> 00:15:44.910
Right now. Immediately!

00:15:44.990 --> 00:15:47.450
If I don't talk to him,
my health will decline!

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:49.580
Because you were...

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:52.290
k-k-kissing her!

00:15:52.750 --> 00:15:55.170
Y-You were watching?
But I didn't kiss her!

00:15:55.250 --> 00:15:56.090
Yes, you did!

00:15:56.290 --> 00:15:57.210
I did not!

00:15:57.300 --> 00:15:59.300
If you're going to watch,
then be focused!

00:15:59.380 --> 00:16:03.930
I'm not a creep! I don't want to watch
people slobber all over each other!

00:16:04.010 --> 00:16:07.970
Slobber? I didn't kiss her!
I was just blowing air.

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:08.970
What?

00:16:10.060 --> 00:16:10.890
Why?

00:16:12.810 --> 00:16:15.690
Natsume's mom taught me.

00:16:15.860 --> 00:16:17.860
When Natsume cried as a baby,

00:16:17.940 --> 00:16:20.690
if you blew air on her nose,
she'd stop crying.

00:16:21.110 --> 00:16:23.990
I was the one who cried today.

00:16:24.110 --> 00:16:27.830
You knew each other from way back then?

00:16:28.950 --> 00:16:29.790
Yeah.

00:16:31.660 --> 00:16:34.250
As people who live to serve Lord Mitatsu,

00:16:34.370 --> 00:16:37.250
we lived in a community together
in the mountains.

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:41.420
The boys go to the Air Self-Defense Force
after graduating high school and college,

00:16:41.800 --> 00:16:46.090
while the girls trained
to become miko during high school.

00:16:47.850 --> 00:16:48.680
Hi, Auntie!

00:16:49.100 --> 00:16:50.220
Oh, Haruto!

00:16:50.640 --> 00:16:52.350
Did you come to meet Natsume?

00:16:54.940 --> 00:16:56.310
Here, hold her.

00:16:56.940 --> 00:16:59.940
She will become
the future Key Girl someday.

00:17:07.910 --> 00:17:09.780
Why don't you try blowing on her nose.

00:17:21.960 --> 00:17:25.220
I've known Natsume since she was a baby.

00:17:25.760 --> 00:17:28.470
She's like my little sister.
That's all.

00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:31.180
Oh, really?

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:32.810
Don't you believe me?

00:17:32.890 --> 00:17:33.850
I do!

00:17:33.930 --> 00:17:36.020
Then why do you still have
that look on your face?

00:17:36.100 --> 00:17:37.520
I don't know!

00:17:37.730 --> 00:17:40.360
It's probably 'cause
I like you, Okonogi!

00:17:46.990 --> 00:17:48.410
Because I like you.

00:17:49.660 --> 00:17:53.290
It's because I like you, Okonogi.

00:17:53.370 --> 00:17:54.700
But that means...

00:17:57.080 --> 00:17:57.920
Amakasu?

00:17:58.210 --> 00:17:59.210
Stop!

00:17:59.710 --> 00:18:04.050
I'm sorry! Right now,
I just need a little more time.

00:18:04.420 --> 00:18:07.880
Sorry, Masotan! I'll come by again!
Excuse me!

00:18:12.010 --> 00:18:13.810
Please let me board Norma.

00:18:14.350 --> 00:18:17.310
What about the possibility
of another anastomosis?

00:18:17.690 --> 00:18:19.940
I will not waver!

00:18:23.150 --> 00:18:26.240
Senior Master Sergeant Hoshino,
you have permission to embark.

00:18:26.650 --> 00:18:27.490
Yes, Ma'am!

00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:32.160
Nao! Sorry I'm late!

00:18:33.870 --> 00:18:35.700
I wonder if she has left already.

00:18:41.460 --> 00:18:43.460
<i>I like Okonogi.</i>

00:18:44.300 --> 00:18:47.630
<i>He's nice, he's got a sweet,</i>
<i>bashful smile...</i>

00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:49.380
<i>and he's nice.</i>

00:18:49.800 --> 00:18:53.350
<i>Even when I misunderstand</i>
<i>and blame him arbitrarily,</i>

00:18:53.510 --> 00:18:57.140
<i>he patiently explains things to me.</i>
<i>He is really nice.</i>

00:18:58.020 --> 00:19:00.230
<i>He cherishes Masotan, too.</i>

00:19:00.900 --> 00:19:01.900
<i>Masotan...</i>

00:19:32.760 --> 00:19:34.930
<i>Maso... tan...</i>

00:19:43.350 --> 00:19:45.690
What clumsy flying.

00:19:46.400 --> 00:19:47.690
Mr. Ikushima.

00:19:47.820 --> 00:19:49.940
Just stumbling at a low altitude.

00:19:50.450 --> 00:19:53.660
However, her ambitions fly higher
than anyone else's.

00:19:54.530 --> 00:19:55.950
<i>Calm down, Sexy Jaguar!</i>

00:19:56.240 --> 00:19:57.790
<i>Maintain formation!</i>

00:19:57.870 --> 00:20:00.210
Sexy Jaguar copies!

00:20:02.170 --> 00:20:03.370
What is this?

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:08.050
A suit I developed earlier in case someone
decided they wanted to ride the OTF.

00:20:08.380 --> 00:20:12.130
-I'm not really a Dragon Pilot.
-This is not used for that purpose.

00:20:12.470 --> 00:20:13.300
Huh?

00:20:13.800 --> 00:20:16.180
It might be impossible
to be used for precise piloting.

00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:21.180
But in terms of maintenance, if it is used
for dispersing an OTF's heat,

00:20:21.270 --> 00:20:23.440
it may be possible to do a short flight.

00:20:24.850 --> 00:20:28.150
The pilot's power alone is not enough
for the flight!

00:20:28.570 --> 00:20:31.190
Because we each have our own powers...

00:20:31.490 --> 00:20:33.610
they can take off into the sky.

00:20:33.910 --> 00:20:36.950
Which means that
by supporting the pilot...

00:20:37.330 --> 00:20:40.200
we can all fly together in the great sky.

00:20:41.250 --> 00:20:43.960
Perhaps it's only me,
but it's what I believe.

00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:47.540
What about you, Kaizaki?

00:20:53.590 --> 00:20:54.680
Nao...

00:20:55.720 --> 00:20:57.720
For me and Masotan...

00:21:00.970 --> 00:21:01.810
She's nice.

00:21:02.560 --> 00:21:03.430
Hisone?

00:21:04.980 --> 00:21:06.980
Nao is nice.

00:21:07.440 --> 00:21:11.820
Mr. Ikushima, Flight Leader Kakiyasu,
and all of the Dragon Pilots, too.

00:21:12.400 --> 00:21:15.030
Everyone on Gifu Air Base is nice.

00:21:17.320 --> 00:21:19.530
Thank you very much, Mr. Ikushima.

00:21:36.800 --> 00:21:38.590
Thank you, Airman 3rd Class Kaizaki.

00:21:38.890 --> 00:21:39.720
Yes, Ma'am.

00:21:39.800 --> 00:21:42.930
Prospects for OTF heat dispersion
are looking brighter.

00:21:43.020 --> 00:21:46.600
But as for the execution
of the Ritual, at this rate...

00:21:46.980 --> 00:21:48.100
High Steward Okonogi.

00:21:48.650 --> 00:21:51.690
How do you feel about
Technical Sergeant Amakasu?

00:21:52.780 --> 00:21:55.400
Kakiyasu, you can't be so direct...

00:21:58.910 --> 00:22:00.660
-I...
-Masotan!

00:22:05.290 --> 00:22:06.120
Amakasu?

00:22:07.040 --> 00:22:07.870
Amakasu.

00:22:08.290 --> 00:22:10.000
Okonogi. Nao.

00:22:10.290 --> 00:22:14.300
Oh, Flight Leader Remi Kakiyasu
and Commander Sosoda were here.

00:22:14.380 --> 00:22:17.630
You've got quite a refreshing
look on your face, Amakasu.

00:22:17.720 --> 00:22:20.800
Yes, I was confused about
many things...

00:22:21.050 --> 00:22:22.640
but my mind is clear now.

00:22:24.060 --> 00:22:24.890
Then?

00:22:25.520 --> 00:22:28.940
Yes. It was a simple answer.

00:22:29.230 --> 00:22:31.150
I... I...

00:22:32.690 --> 00:22:35.940
I will quit the Dragon Pilots
and the Air Self-Defense Force!

00:22:36.240 --> 00:22:38.950
TO BE CONTINUED

00:24:09.870 --> 00:24:11.960
<i>-Going out for drinks.</i>
<i>-Oh my God!</i>

00:24:12.040 --> 00:24:14.250
<i>Trading sides dishes we didn't like.</i>

00:24:14.630 --> 00:24:17.250
<i>-Going to the movies.</i>
<i>-You're kidding, right?</i>

00:24:17.340 --> 00:24:18.670
<i>All of it.</i>

00:24:18.750 --> 00:24:20.300
<i>What is she doing?</i>

00:24:21.050 --> 00:24:22.800
<i>Shut up, you piece of trash!</i>
